{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "All three load-bearing artifacts describe the same trip: trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown each carry trip_id TRP-00515, and the timestamps cohere (accepted 17:30:40, started 17:36:40, first GPS fix 17:36:40, ended/last fix 18:37:40). The rider's threshold case under POL-RD-08(a) is therefore made out, and the booked optimal route on the trip record is 34.2 km and 40.0 minutes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00515", "EV-GPS-00515", "EV-FARE-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The governing distance is the trace figure, not the rounded trip-record copy. POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km (48.82 km) govern where it disagrees with trip_record.actual_distance_km (48.8 km), and the trip-record field may not be cited for the threshold test. Measured on the governing figure against the 34.2 km optimal, the excess is 14.62 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00515", "EV-TRIP-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The deviation is established on both limbs of POL-RD-01: an excess of 14.62 km is more than 20% of the 34.2 km optimal (the 20% line is 6.84 km) and more than 0.8 km in absolute terms. The trace reports the excess as 42.75% of optimal.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The deviation is additionally MATERIAL: an excess of 14.62 km exceeds the 8.0 km absolute materiality threshold set out in POL-RD-01, which in turn requires the driver_profile check under POL-RD-06.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is clean for policy purposes. It carries 367 fixes at a 10 s interval against an expected 10 s, no gaps at all, max_gap_sec 0.0 and 100% coverage. It meets none of limbs (a) to (c) of POL-RD-07, so no impairment discount applies, the measured excess is the excess, and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation is engaged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver has no admissible exculpation. His statement blames a confusing KPE split and an admission that he missed it, but he cites no advisory. The bundle's only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00515-01, is MISSING: status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. POL-RD-03 cannot be run without a named corridor and validity window, and under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13 the assertion carries no weight; the measured excess therefore stands unreduced.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00515-01", "EV-GPS-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There was no rider-requested detour. The chat log holds exactly one message, the rider asking the driver to put the phone down, with waypoint_hint null and no road or place named. POL-RD-04 requires a rider instruction that identifies a waypoint or road and is corroborated by the vehicle passing within 200 m of it; neither exists here, so the clause is unavailable to the driver and no part of the excess is excluded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00515", "EV-GPS-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The optimal baseline is the booked optimal of 34.2 km. This trip is RYDE_PLUS, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline and its co-rider exclusion do not apply and cannot be used to explain any part of the 14.62 km excess away.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12", "POL-RD-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "A repeat deviation pattern is established under POL-RD-06. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 3, which meets the clause's threshold of 3 or more, against 180 completed trips in the same window (well above the 40-trip floor). Under POL-GEN-01 the claim rests on those two named fields only and on no other profile field.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the POL-RD-06 pattern is established, and because this deviation is both MATERIAL and substantiated on this trip's own trace, limb (b) uplifts the remedy from the POL-RD-02 partial to FULL_REFUND of charged_total. The two figures printed side by side, as the clause requires: POL-RD-02 standing alone yields SGD 20.85 (charged_total 62.28 less recomputed_fare 41.45, rounded up); the uplifted outcome is the entire charged_total of SGD 62.28 — SGD 58.28 of distance, time and platform charges uplifted by this limb, plus the SGD 4.00 of off-route ERP which POL-RD-09 settles on its own footing and which this limb does not need to uplift.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00515", "EV-DPROF-00515", "EV-GPS-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the uplift is declined, the ordinary POL-RD-02 arithmetic still runs: recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 34.2 + 0.28 x 40.0) x 1.0 surge + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP on the optimal route = 41.45; refund = 62.28 - 41.45 = 20.83, rounded up to SGD 20.85 payable. The fare_model is METERED, not UPFRONT_QUOTE, so POL-RD-02 and not POL-RD-11 governs, and the surge multiplier is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, which is 1.0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The SGD 4.00 of ERP is wholly off-route: both charged gantries, TPE (Seletar Link towards Punggol) and TPE (Punggol Rd towards Tampines), carry on_optimal_route = false, and each is matched to a trace fix at 0 m. Under POL-RD-09 these pass-through lines travel with the deviation refund, are itemised separately in the ruling, and are never added on top of the distance-and-time figure a second time.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00515", "EV-GPS-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.off_optimal_route_total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's account is corroborated beyond the trace, so the case is not a trace-only case. At 17:48:40, twelve minutes into the trip, the rider messaged 'can you please put the phone down and drive', and the driver's own counter-statement concedes 'I was checking the navigation on my phone'. That combination supports the POL-RD-06(c) referral to driver-conduct review, which is recorded in the ruling's referrals list and does not displace or delay the monetary outcome.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries no adverse claim history that would add a corroboration burden. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so the POL-RD-08 rider-side trigger (4 or more claims with 1 or fewer substantiated) does not fire, and the ordinary burden is discharged on this trip's own trace. Under POL-GEN-01 no other rider profile field bears on the outcome.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00515", "EV-GPS-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Under POL-RD-01 the governing distance figure is the trace, gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 48.82 km, not the rounded trip_record convenience copy of 48.8 km. Measured against the 34.2 km booked optimal, the excess is 14.62 km, or 42.75 percent. That is the whole of the departure the rider can point to: 34.2 of the 48.8 km driven was the optimal route, so a claim to the entire 62.28 SGD fare is not supported by this trip's own measurement.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00515", "EV-TRIP-00515", "EV-FARE-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's account of a driver 'driving slowly so he could keep scrolling' is contradicted by the driver's own trace: 367 fixes at a 10 s cadence record sustained speeds clustered in the 45-50 kph band with a single low reading of 4.4 kph, and the trace carries no hard-braking or lane-drift signature at all. The narrative, not the data, is doing the work in that part of the claim.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip ran 61 minutes against a 40-minute optimal - 21 minutes over, not the 'forty minutes became ninety' of the claim - and the only in-app message on the trip is the rider's own, sent at 17:48:40. Under POL-RD-02 the recomputation runs on optimal_duration_min = 40.0 against the recording engine's duration, not against the rider's account of the journey.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00515", "EV-CHAT-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "payload.actual_duration_min",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The substance of the claim - phone use, two hard brakes, lane drift and the rider's fear - is a conduct complaint. No line of the fare_breakdown prices conduct, and the route-deviation policy's only monetary remedy is the arithmetic recomputation in POL-RD-02. Under POL-GEN-03 the ruling moves the figure that arithmetic produces for a route deviation and nothing more; conduct is a referral matter, not a fare line.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00515", "EV-TRIP-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is clean for policy purposes: 367 fixes at a 10 s cadence, 100 percent coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0 s. POL-RD-07(a) to (c) is therefore not engaged, the trace is not impaired for policy purposes, and there is no POL-RD-10(3) escalation available on this bundle.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "payload.max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Both charged ERP gantries carry a trace fix at 0 m - well inside the 250 m match radius POL-RD-09 uses - so both gantries were crossed by this vehicle. Neither line is a phantom crossing: there is no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity finding to record and no POL-RD-10(8) escalation on this bundle.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00515", "EV-FARE-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 4.00 SGD of off-route ERP is already comprehended in the fare refund under POL-RD-09(1) and must never be added on top of it. The driver's exposure on this trip is one figure, not a sum made of a distance refund plus the gantry lines itemised a second time.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00515", "EV-GPS-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.off_optimal_route_total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The meter was not inflated. The distance charged, 48.8 km, matches the 48.82 km the trace records, and the time charged, 61.0 minutes, matches the trip record; the fare model on this trip is METERED, so the billed lines are the trace lines. The driver billed no more distance or time than the trace shows he drove, so the rider is not paying for padded meter movement.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00515", "EV-GPS-00515", "EV-TRIP-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "payload.distance_charged_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Any POL-RD-06 pattern finding must rest on driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d alone: POL-GEN-01 makes prior_deviation_flags - 5 on this profile - a lifetime counter that is context only and cannot be substituted for the trailing-90-day figure the clause names, and the trailing-window rate here is 3 of 180 trips, 1.67 percent, far below the clause's 5 percent limb. Any uplift under POL-RD-06(b) is an uplift on the remedy, not on the finding, and it does not touch the government and third-party pass-through lines, which are settled once under POL-RD-09.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00515", "EV-FARE-00515"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01", "POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 62.28,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-06(c): refer the driver to driver-conduct review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "The route-deviation claim is made out. All three load-bearing artifacts — trip record EV-TRIP-00515, GPS trace EV-GPS-00515 and fare breakdown EV-FARE-00515 — carry trip_id TRP-00515 and cohere in time (accepted 17:30:40, started/first fix 17:36:40, ended/last fix 18:37:40), so the rider's threshold burden under POL-RD-08(a) is discharged. On the governing distance figure — the trace, trace_distance_km 48.82 km, which POL-RD-01 makes govern over the rounded trip-record copy of 48.8 km — the excess over the 34.2 km booked optimal is 14.62 km, or 42.75%. That passes both POL-RD-01 establishment limbs (20% of 34.2 km = 6.84 km; absolute floor 0.8 km) and also exceeds the 8.0 km materiality threshold, so this is a MATERIAL deviation. The driver's point that the raw measurement does not, by itself, support a claim to the whole fare is correct and is the starting point of the arithmetic below; it is not the end of the case. The trace is clean for policy purposes: 367 fixes at a 10 s cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0, so POL-RD-07(a)–(c) is not engaged and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises. The driver's accusation of slow driving is not supported by the trace either (sustained speeds of 45–50 kph), but that cuts against the conduct narrative only, not the route finding. No exculpatory clause runs. The driver's statement blames a confusing KPE split and admits he missed it once — an admission of driver error, not an external traffic cause — and in any event the bundle holds no traffic advisory: EV-ADVIS-00515-01 is MISSING at weight_multiplier 0.0 (issue MISSING_ARTIFACT). Under POL-RD-13 and POL-RD-08 that assertion is tested against the advisory and carries no weight, and POL-RD-03 is unavailable. Because the driver named no advisory evidence ID, POL-RD-13(1) applies and the missing advisory is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. POL-RD-04 is unavailable: the single chat message (17:48:40, 'can you please put the phone down and drive') has waypoint_hint null and names no road or place. POL-RD-05 does not run (no amendment timestamps). POL-RD-12 does not apply (vehicle_type RYDE_PLUS, not RYDE_POOL), so the 34.2 km booked optimal is the correct baseline. The POL-RD-02 arithmetic, on its own line: recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 × 34.2 + 0.28 × 40.0) × surge 1.0 (read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP on the optimal route = 41.45; refund = charged_total 62.28 − 41.45 = 20.83, rounded UP to SGD 20.85. The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-11 does not apply, and the meter was not inflated (48.8 km billed against 48.82 km traced; 61.0 min billed against the record), so there is no billing-integrity defect and no POL-RD-09(4) referral. The POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is required by the MATERIAL finding, and a repeat deviation pattern is established: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 3, meeting the clause's '3 or more' limb, against 180 completed trips in the window. The driver is right that the trailing-window rate (3/180 = 1.67%) is below the clause's 5% limb and that prior_deviation_flags (5) is a lifetime counter POL-GEN-01 makes context-only and inadmissible for this test — but the clause is disjunctive and the count limb alone establishes the pattern, so the driver's narrower reading does not defeat it. Under POL-RD-06(b) the remedy is uplifted from the POL-RD-02 partial to FULL_REFUND of the charged total. Stated side by side as the clause requires: POL-RD-02 standing alone yields SGD 20.85; the uplifted figure is the charged_total of SGD 62.28, of which SGD 58.28 (distance, time and platform charges) is uplifted by this limb and SGD 4.00 of off-route ERP is settled under POL-RD-09 rather than uplifted. Both charged gantries (TPE Seletar Link, SGD 2.00; TPE Punggol Rd, SGD 2.00) are matched to trace fixes at 0 m and carry on_optimal_route = false; they are itemised for transparency and are comprehended in the award, never added on top a second time. The conduct complaints (phone use, hard braking, lane drift) are not priced by any fare line and do not change the money; they are answered through the POL-RD-06(c) referral below, which the established pattern produces and which does not displace or delay this monetary ruling. The counterparty statement carries no weight_multiplier and so enters neither the minimum nor the maximum of the POL-GEN-02(2) cap; it is evidence, and its admissions of phone use and of missing the split are noted, but they carry no fare consequence. All facts this ruling rests on are carried by artifacts at weight_multiplier 1.0 (trace, trip record, fare breakdown, driver profile), so the cap is 1.0 and confidence is set at 0.85.",
    "confidence_note": null
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
